      "writtenOn": "2022-06-13T22:07:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I find it confusing to use the shared signal listener. So instead I set up this in `main.rs`:\n```\n    // There are multiple signal handlers. We need to set signal match mode to true to allow signal\n    // handlers process the signals independently. Otherwise only the first signal handler will get\n    // the chance to handle the same signal in case the match rule overlaps.\n    conn.set_signal_match_mode(true);\n```\nSo that each signal handler can handle the signals independenty, therefore always returning \"true\".",
      "parentUuid": "dc734d92_1eddc961",
      "revId": "bf42d014ef623edb109806c01dbcd3bb92bb514d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d9a3f3f2_c3ca1159",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/mgmt/src/service_watcher.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 214,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-13T22:11:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of the value true, we should use an Enum that evaluates to true\n\n```\nenum SignalAction {\n  Continue,\n  Stop,\n}\n\nimpl From\u003cSignalAction\u003e for bool {\n  fn from(item: SignalAction) -\u003e Self {\n    match item {\n      SignalAction::Continue \u003d\u003e true,\n      SignalAction::Stop \u003d\u003e false,\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n```",
      "parentUuid": "0cea24cd_1d6ad360",
      "revId": "bf42d014ef623edb109806c01dbcd3bb92bb514d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
